I have (I fear /had/) a very promising game going.
I just moved downstairs (to dlvl 24) and received the following
set of messages:

placing defunct monster onto map?  Program in disorder - perhaps you'd better #quit.
It touches you!  A monster appears from nowhere!  dmonsfree: 1 removed doesn't match 0 pending  Program in disorder - perhaps you'd better #quit.

The "placing defunct monster onto map?" message appears to come from 
steed.c line 632, which makes me think it has something to do
with my pet (a warhorse, which had shortly before gotten polymorphed
into a centaur).  The relevant function for the second message
begins at mons.c line 1244.  There are a couple of bugfixes that seem
to relate to something similar listed in fixes34.1.

Is this a known issue?  What can I do to track this down? Does anyone
have ideas on what else might be relevant?

More importantly, is my game trashed? This is the first bug
I've ever encountered in Nethack, in several years of playing.

Thanks.




